Package: a-nas-host
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: A-NAS <zhongwater123@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: acl, btrfs-progs, parted, smartmontools, samba, iproute2, udev, systemd, python3, ffmpeg, heif-thumbnailer, libheif-plugin-libde265, libegl1, libgles2, libgomp1, libssl3t64, @UPSTREAM@, nftables, wireguard-tools, a-nas-archive-keyring (>= @VERSION@)
Description: what an A-NAS device needs from Debian and upstream
 The Host Agent, the Product Service and their workers run these commands
 and link these libraries. The a-nas package requires this package at the
 version of the release it installs (docs/adr/0031). Caddy serves the LAN
 entry (docs/adr/0012) and, with WireGuard and nftables, the internet entry
 (docs/adr/0032); Docker runs the App Center's apps. Caddy and Docker are the
 upstream packages that A-NAS's repository carries, at least at the versions
 deploy/upstream/packages.json pins for this release (docs/adr/0015). The
 internet entry and the App Center stay off until their runbooks turn them
 on. Each release brings the keyring it was signed for, so a revoked or added
 subkey of the archive key reaches the device with the next upgrade.
